    <string name="rules_title">How to play</string>
    <string name="welcome_title">Welcome. Three steps.</string>
    <string name="rules_1">Pick a peg, pinch. The bead does the sliding.</string>
    <string name="rules_2">Pinch the same peg again to drop. One click per layer.</string>
    <string name="rules_3">Any four in a line wins, even through the layers. Push the rim to turn it.</string>
    <string name="rules_mistakes">Common slips</string>
    <string name="mistake_1">Don\'t stare at one layer. Cross-layer diagonals sneak up on you. Look at every line that lights up.</string>
    <string name="mistake_2">Your bead is its stepping stone. Check the spot right above before you drop.</string>
    <string name="mistake_3">The middle four pegs are worth the most, then the corners. Don\'t open on the edges.</string>
    <string name="rules_drag">Drag the tower onto your table. It reads best from above.</string>
    <string name="rules_hard">Why does Hard let you go first? First player has a winning line in this game. It\'s giving you the shot.</string>
    <string name="rules_pvp">Two players: eye tracking stays tuned to the first person. The controller is steadier.</string>
